republic-overreach.logic.r2: argue/equivocates: P8 (S39): "go beyond" is taken as grasping for more gain or advantage than others (the pleonexia Thrasymachus credits to the unjust) in P8 P9 and as wanting to outdo others in a skill or practice (e.g. tuning a lyre past what another musician does) where exceeds_like is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C (S44) does not follow (republic-overreach.logic.r2.sense1)
republic-overreach.logic.r2: argue/countermodel: C (S44): D = {just, unjust}; bad = ∅, exceeds_like = ∅, exceeds_like_2 = {unjust}, exceeds_unlike = {just, unjust}, good = ∅, ignorant = ∅, like_evil_ignorant = ∅, like_wise_good = {just, unjust}, wise = ∅
republic-overreach.logic.r2: argue/equivocates: P8 (S39): "go beyond" is taken as grasping for more gain or advantage than others in P8 P9 and as wanting to outdo others in a skill or practice where exceeds_unlike is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C (S44) does not follow (republic-overreach.logic.r2.sense2)
republic-overreach.logic.r2: argue/countermodel: C (S44): D = {just, unjust}; bad = ∅, exceeds_like = {unjust}, exceeds_unlike = ∅, exceeds_unlike_2 = {just, unjust}, good = ∅, ignorant = ∅, like_evil_ignorant = ∅, like_wise_good = ∅, wise = ∅
republic-overreach.logic.r2: argue/equivocates: A3: it takes "go beyond" from grasping for more gain or advantage to wanting to outdo others in a skill or practice, a reader says: the argument holds only through it; without it, C (S44) does not follow (republic-overreach.logic.r2.sense3)
republic-overreach.logic.r2: argue/countermodel: C (S44): D = {another, just, unjust}; bad = ∅, exceeds_like = {unjust}, exceeds_unlike = {just, unjust}, good = ∅, ignorant = ∅, like_evil_ignorant = {unjust}, like_wise_good = ∅, wise = ∅
republic-overreach.logic.r2: argue/equivocates: A4: it takes "go beyond" from grasping for more gain or advantage to wanting to outdo others in a skill or practice, a reader says: the argument holds only through it; without it, C (S44) does not follow (republic-overreach.logic.r2.sense4)
republic-overreach.logic.r2: argue/countermodel: C (S44): D = {another, just, unjust}; bad = ∅, exceeds_like = {unjust}, exceeds_unlike = {just, unjust}, good = ∅, ignorant = ∅, like_evil_ignorant = ∅, like_wise_good = {just}, wise = ∅
